WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.775
Mastery Starter 9.0.

00:00:02.775 --> 00:00:05.100
New to DeFi vs Grid Bots?

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.160
Start here.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.247
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:08.247 --> 00:00:09.940
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.182
A grid bot on an exchange and a liquidity

00:00:14.182 --> 00:00:17.123
position on a DEX both buy as price falls

00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:19.945
and sell as it rises inside a range.

00:00:19.945 --> 00:00:22.620
This module shows when each is the better tool,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.240
and how to run both without doubling your risk.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:31.020
Grid bot: automated buy/sell orders at set price levels.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.915
Range: the price band a strategy works in.

00:00:33.915 --> 00:00:38.652
Concentrated liquidity: LP capital placed in a chosen range.

00:00:38.652 --> 00:00:41.492
Correlation: positions that move together.

00:00:41.492 --> 00:00:44.820
Invalidation: the event that ends a range thesis.

00:00:46.121 --> 00:00:50.351
Modules 0–8 (Grid Bot Builder helpful but not required).

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:54.124
Take one asset and write the range you'd

00:00:54.124 --> 00:00:55.933
use for a grid bot and for an

00:00:55.933 --> 00:00:57.561
LP. Would they be the same?

00:00:58.861 --> 00:01:02.311
Beginner: Explains the grid–LP similarity.

00:01:02.311 --> 00:01:04.625
Practitioner: Chooses the right tool

00:01:04.625 --> 00:01:06.551
by size, custody and pair.

00:01:06.551 --> 00:01:09.356
Master: Runs grid bots and DeFi as one

00:01:09.356 --> 00:01:12.808
system with exposure counted by asset and range.

00:01:14.108 --> 00:01:17.062
You've mastered this module when your exposure

00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:19.702
is counted by underlying asset and range,

00:01:19.702 --> 00:01:21.399
not by number of positions.

00:01:22.699 --> 00:01:25.214
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:25.214 --> 00:01:29.134
Next up, Lesson 9.1: Same idea, different machine.
